RccExtended 1.0.6-2 — local Arch repair candidate
===============================================

License: GPL-3.0-only WITH Qt-GPL-exception-1.0. The author's license clarification
and notices are backported from commit eea2824a; see LICENSE-STATUS.txt.
RELEASE REVIEW PENDING: three clean-chroot passes and Danny's approval remain.
No publication or host installation has been authorized.

The program is installed as rccextended, leaving Qt's /usr/bin/rcc untouched.
It can inspect binary Qt resource bundles without launching their application.
It is not a general executable decompiler or a sandbox.

In a fresh, writable working directory:

    rccextended --reverse -- /absolute/path/to/example.rcc
    sh qresource/rcc/rcc-make.sh

Extraction is explicit; the program never runs the generated rebuild script.
Review that script and the generated QRC before running it. Normal QRC compiler
mode reads the source files named in its input; use only trusted QRC projects.
Use a rootless, network-isolated sandbox for unfamiliar resource bundles.

The reverse command accepts multiple files and quoted wildcard patterns. It
returns nonzero for missing/invalid input, failed writes or unsupported resources.
It refuses any existing qresource path, including symlinks. It stages results in
a private directory and exposes qresource only after the whole batch succeeds.
Failures discard only the new staging directory, not an earlier extraction.

Output layout:

    qresource/res/<full-input-basename>/<language-id>_<country-id>/<resource-path>
    qresource/qrc/<full-input-basename>.qrc
    qresource/rcc/rcc-make.sh
    qresource/log.txt

Numeric locale directories avoid collisions with genuine resource paths.
Aliases and supported locale values are retained in escaped XML. Rebuild scripts
quote filenames as literals and work after moving the complete output directory.
They use rccextended from PATH. Rebuilding preserves file contents/aliases/locales,
not original binary layout, compression choice, timestamps or byte identity.
Two inputs with the same basename are rejected, even from different directories.

Intentional limits: RCC formats 1–3 in Qt's header/payload/name/tree layout;
64 MiB per input and per expanded file; 256 MiB total expanded output per run;
10,000 tree nodes across the whole batch; directory depth 64; resource components at most
255 UTF-8 bytes and resource paths at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes. Unsafe path components,
invalid XML/UTF-16 names, duplicate alias/locale pairs, inconsistent trees and
unrepresentable Qt 5 locales are rejected. Larger/nonstandard bundles need review,
not removal of the checks. OS path-length and filesystem errors still fail safely.

Validation:

    python check.py /absolute/path/to/rccextended

The standard-library checker requires Qt's rcc and ShellCheck. It uses synthetic
temporary inputs, no network, no models and no credentials. Run candidate code
only as an ordinary user in isolation. Rootless host-library diagnostics are not
clean-chroot verification; three clean-chroot passes and Danny's review remain.
